# Cloudflare Pages routing for Plotted.
#
# THE ONE LINE THAT MATTERS
#
# `/api/*` has to reach the API on the **same origin as the page**. The refresh
# token is an HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookie scoped to /api/v1/auth, and a
# cross-origin split does not fail cleanly -- the browser simply declines to send
# the cookie, so sessions stop persisting and it presents as random sign-outs
# rather than as a configuration error. That is the single most likely thing to
# be subtly wrong on a first deploy.
#
# Replace PLOTTED_API_HOST below with the Cloud Run URL before uploading. It is
# a placeholder rather than a real host because this file is committed and the
# host is not known until the API is deployed.
#
# 200 rather than 301/302: a redirect would change the origin in the address
# bar, which is exactly what this exists to prevent.

/api/*  https://PLOTTED_API_HOST/api/:splat  200

# Angular is a single-page app: every non-asset path has to serve index.html or a
# refresh on /watchlist returns 404 from the static host. Last rule, so it does
# not shadow the proxy above.

/*  /index.html  200
